{"attempted": true, "categories": ["讨论关系", "否定", "限制", "代码"], "changes_understanding": "no", "client": "gtx", "code_intact": "yes", "comment_body_sha256": "c238ee251bfdd0e86acbb4c6d127f3fe92a0686d183b34c12e5306ebf1495cc6", "comment_id": 124570444, "discussion_kept": "yes", "elapsed_ms": 288, "endpoint_host": "translate.googleapis.com", "error_class": "无", "error_detail": "", "error_location": "无", "fetched_at": "2026-09-22T02:05:26Z", "frag_id": "P-06", "frozen_at": "2026-09-22T02:05:13Z", "http_status": 200, "judge": "w6-technical-check", "judged_at": "2026-09-22T02:06:51Z", "lang_pair": "en→zh", "limit_kept": "yes", "line_end": null, "line_start": null, "must_keep": ["git fsck", "git"], "notes": "more trouble than not 收成了“会造成更多麻烦”，比较对象没有了；but 和不修的决定还在。反引号变成中文引号，git fsck 与 git 文本还在。这句不记成严重误译。", "polarity_kept": "yes", "risk_note": "先承认技术上可能并表示若不影响历史就会支持，再用 but 转到不修；后段命令名须保留。", "severe_mistranslation": "no", "source_kind": "issue_comment", "source_lang": "en", "source_path": null, "source_repo": "psf/requests", "source_sha": null, "source_sha256": "c238ee251bfdd0e86acbb4c6d127f3fe92a0686d183b34c12e5306ebf1495cc6", "source_text": "To be clear, it is _technically_ possible to repair this, also if repairing it didn't affect the repository's history from that point on, I would be very much in favor of it, but it irrevocably breaks expectations around our history and will cause more trouble than not. You appear to be the first person to have checked this and found it to be an issue.\n\nEven if `git fsck` reports the commit as being damaged, `git` continues to work just fine. This doesn't realistically affect the use of the repository or any person's ability to contribute to it. I appreciate you reporting this, but it simply isn't something we're going to fix.\n", "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/2690#issuecomment-124570444", "target_lang": "zh-CN", "terminology_kept": "不适用", "tool": "google-translate-gtx", "tool_version": "未知", "translation_output": "需要明确的是，从技术上讲，修复此问题是可能的，而且如果修复它不会影响存储库从那时起的历史记录，我会非常支持它，但它不可挽回地打破了对我们历史记录的期望，并且会造成更多麻烦。您似乎是第一个检查此问题并发现这是一个问题的人。\n\n即使“git fsck”报告提交已损坏，“git”仍然可以正常工作。这实际上并不会影响存储库的使用或任何人为其做出贡献的能力。感谢您报告此问题，但这根本不是我们要解决的问题。"}
